  "summary": "Mutant League Football is Mutant Productions' sports game, released by Electronic Arts for Genesis in North America in May 1993.",
  "body": [
    "Mutant League Football is Mutant Productions' sports game, released by Electronic Arts for Genesis in North America in May 1993. It adapts the machinery of Madden NFL '93 to teams of monstrous players and fields filled with hazards. Recognisable football plays coexist with skeletons, aliens, land mines and other ways to lose a player permanently. The basic goal still involves moving the ball and scoring, but the match also becomes a struggle to keep enough of the team alive to continue playing at all.",
    "Players have health, and collisions or environmental hazards can kill them during a match. Losing a member of the team can change a useful play into a dangerous decision, especially on a field with pits or explosives. Special Nasty Audibles let the team introduce additional tricks, including an exploding ball. Those options turn the ordinary preparation before a snap into another opportunity to interfere with the opposition. The sporting structure remains readable, while each field and malicious adjustment creates a new risk around an otherwise familiar movement of the ball.",
    "A coach can bribe the referee into penalising the opposing team, whose response may involve killing that official and facing a more demanding replacement. A team that loses too many players can forfeit, making elimination another route to victory. Exhibition games and a season mode give the violence a recognisable competition to unfold within, accompanied by Brian Schmidt's music. The joke works through the relationship between the two systems: football provides the rules and expectations, then the monsters, hazards and dirty tricks make following the next play wonderfully unreliable."
  ],
  "story_headings": [
    "Football on a dangerous field",
    "A play with another purpose",
    "Winning by surviving"
  ],
